scripts/migrations/data_20260822020737_2026-08-22-record-correction-and-biblio-repair.sql:20:UPDATE "evidence_sources" SET "tier" = 3, "notes" = ' || SCOPE LIMIT recorded 2026-08-19 (adversarial L5): this study manipulates sound LEVEL only (silence / 40 dB / 75 dB, lab-presented). It contains no RT60, NRC, STC or NC value. Independent of population it cannot anchor any room-acoustic performance figure on this slug. || SCOPE DELIBERATELY LEFT NULL 2026-08-22, and this is a REFERRAL, not an oversight. evidence_type=''clinical'' admits TWO scopes under the ratified table: high_control -> Tier 1, lower_control -> Tier 3. The stored tier is 1, so writing scope=''high_control'' would make the record self-consistent — and would harden, by a clerical act, exactly the tier the 2026-08-20 adversarial pass disputes. Its argument: an n=27 single-centre observational EEG study whose own note here concedes it ''contains no RT60, NRC, STC or NC value'' is defensibly T3, i.e. lower_control. That is owner decision OD-E (workplan/2026-08-22-agonist-antagonist-execution-plan.md section 2). Until it is answered, adjudication_integrity.py will keep reporting ONE inconsistency here, and it should: the gate is pointing at a real open question, which is what a gate is for. || TIER RE-GRADED 1 -> 3 on 2026-08-22 by OWNER DECISION OD-E, recorded in workplan/2026-08-22-agonist-antagonist-execution-plan.md section 2. Evidence-tier definitions are the DG-NON class and this was not a session''s call to make. scope=''lower_control'' is written in the same act because scope is the derivation INPUT, not a consequence: schemas/tier_derivation.py maps (''clinical'',''lower_control'') -> Tier 3, so the stored tier is now DERIVABLE from the ratified table rather than asserted. The prior state was tier=1 with scope NULL, i.e. a tier that no ratified rule could produce. The reasoning the owner adopted, from the 2026-08-20 adversarial pass: an n=27 single-centre observational EEG study is lower_control, not high_control, and this source''s own note here already concedes it ''contains no RT60, NRC, STC or NC value'' -- so independent of population it cannot anchor any room-acoustic performance figure on this slug. Nothing downstream is invalidated: evidence_population_match rows MB1-006 (NDV PARTIAL) and MB1-007 (AUT MISMATCH) grade population, not tier, and specifications is empty, so no determination inherited the old grade. CONSEQUENCE WORTH STATING: with this row at T3, the only Tier-1 evidence on this slug is the three Co-1 rows, whose Co-1 warrant is itself under OD-D.', "scope" = 'lower_control' WHERE "ref_id" = 'REF-00967';
scripts/migrations/data_20260822021003_2026-08-22-record-correction-and-biblio-repair.sql:13:INSERT INTO decisions (decision_id, category, delegation, delegation_rationale, summary, outcome, rationale, decision_date, decided_by, model_routing, effort_level, status, review_status, supersedes, predecessors, decision_artifacts, alternatives_considered, notes, created_at, created_by_session, updated_at, updated_by_session) VALUES ('D-0166', 'D-DOCT', 'DG-NON', 'Evidence-tier definitions and their application to a specific source are named in the DG-NON list. Owner ruling of 2026-08-22, taken as OD-E.', 'REF-00967 (Bagheri, Good & Alavi 2024, EEG study of visual and acoustic discomfort in adults with and without ADHD) is re-graded from Tier 1 to Tier 3, with scope=''lower_control''.', 'ADOPTED by owner ruling 2026-08-22 (OD-E). Applied by migration data_20260822020737. adjudication_integrity.py went from FAIL (5 tier-derivation inconsistencies of 5) to PASS (0).', 'Two defects in one row. The tier was over-graded: an n=27 single-centre observational EEG study is lower_control, not high_control, and the source''s own stored note already conceded it ''contains no RT60, NRC, STC or NC value'', so independent of population it cannot anchor any room-acoustic figure on this slug. And the tier was UNDERIVABLE: scope was NULL, and schemas/tier_derivation.py keys the ratified table on (evidence_type, scope), so the stored Tier 1 was an assertion no ratified rule could produce. Writing scope=''lower_control'' supplies the derivation input and the ratified table then yields Tier 3 -- the tier is now derived rather than asserted. Raised by the 2026-08-20 adversarial pass under lens L4 and referred rather than corrected, because tier definitions are not a session''s call.', '2026-08-22', 'jordanelias', 'opus', 'standard', 'ACTIVE', 'NA', '[]', '[]', '["scripts/migrations/data_20260822020737_2026-08-22-record-correction-and-biblio-repair.sql", "workplan/2026-08-20-adversarial-adjudication-a18-aut.md"]', '["Keep Tier 1 with scope=''high_control'' -- defensible on the ground that it is a controlled lab study with a comparison group; would have cleared the same gate by confirming the stored tier.", "Leave scope NULL until the full text is read -- would have kept the gate reporting one inconsistency, which was the honest interim state and is what the session held before the ruling."]', 'OD-D remains OPEN and is the larger half of the same question: the 2026-08-20 pass also graded REF-00965 and REF-00968 as T3 rather than Co-1, on the ground that no co-production, participatory or DPO warrant is visible in the retrieved record. Resolving it needs full texts this environment cannot reach. If sustained, tier_basis=''Co-1'' on this slug rests on ONE source (REF-00966), not three. With REF-00967 now at T3, the only Tier-1 evidence on room-acoustic-performance is those three Co-1 rows -- so OD-D determines whether the slug has any Tier-1 anchor at all.', '2026-08-22', 'session_2026-08-22-record-correction-and-biblio-repair', '2026-08-22', 'session_2026-08-22-record-correction-and-biblio-repair');
